## Intuition
- The key idea is to examine each digit of the number one by one and keep track of the largest digit encountered so far.
- We can extract the last digit of a number using n % 10. After processing that digit, we remove it using n /= 10.
- By repeating this process until all digits are processed, we can find the largest digit.

## Approach
1. Initialize mx = 0 to store the largest digit found so far.
1. Run a loop while n > 0.
1. Extract the last digit using:
1. int digit = n % 10; 
1. Compare the current digit with mx and update mx:
1. mx = max(mx, digit);
1. Remove the last digit using:
1. n /= 10;
1. Continue until all digits have been processed.
1. Return mx.

