## Intuition
To find the largest digit, extract digits one by one from right to left using the modulo operator (% 10), compare each digit with a running maximum, and remove the last digit using integer division (/ 10) until the number becomes 0.

## Approach
1. Initialize a variable max = 0 to store the maximum digit encountered.

2. Run a while loop as long as n > 0.

3. Extract the last digit using int temp = n % 10.

4. If temp > max, update max = temp.

5. Reduce n by dividing it by 10 (n = n / 10).

6. Return max after the loop terminates.

## Solution
```java[]
class Solution {
    public int largestDigit(int n) {
        int max = 0;
        while(n>0){
            int temp = n%10;
            if(temp>max){
                max = temp;
            }
            n = n/10;
        }
        return max;
    }
}
```

## Complexity
**Time Complexity:**
O(log₁₀(n)) — The number of digits in n determines the number of iterations.

**Space Complexity:**
O(1) — Uses a constant amount of extra memory.

